    <section class="os-why">
      <h2 class="os-why-head">You already know how this goes.</h2>
      <div class="os-why-list">
        <p class="os-why-t">You spent months building it. Copying it took an afternoon and cost whoever did it nothing &mdash; and every copy that spreads from there is a sale that <em>was yours</em>.</p>
        <p class="os-why-t">A release goes out. Somewhere it has already been taken apart and passed along. The hard part was never that it happens &mdash; it's that you are the <em>last to know</em>.</p>
        <p class="os-why-t">Given enough time, a copy always gets out. The only thing left worth deciding is whether it traces back to no one &mdash; or back to <em>exactly who let it go</em>.</p>
      </div>
      <p class="os-why-close">Software worth building is software worth taking &mdash; that part was never yours to decide. How hard it is <em>to take is</em>.</p>
    </section>

